# .trivyignore - accepted HIGH/CRITICAL findings for freeunit-drupal
#
# Every entry below is either (a) inherited from the freeunit-php base image,
# where it is already audited and suppressed (see that repo's .trivyignore for
# the per-CVE rationale), or (b) introduced by this image's own APT layer and
# analyzed here. All Debian entries have NO fix available at the scan date
# (status "affected" or "fix_deferred", empty FixedVersion) - there is nothing
# to upgrade to. They are acknowledged so the scan surfaces only NEW,
# actionable issues instead of a permanent unfixable backlog.
#
# Trivy reads this file automatically (default ./.trivyignore), so both
# `make scan` and the CI trivy step honour it with no extra flags.
#
# Last audit: 2026-07-17
# REVIEW BY:  2026-10-17 - re-scan and drop any CVE that upstream has since
#             fixed (a fixed CVE left here would silence a real regression).
#             New CVEs are NOT covered until added here.

# =============================================================
# Inherited from the freeunit-php base image.
# Audited upstream; kept in sync with the base's .trivyignore.
# CVEs newer than the base's last audit are analyzed here in place.
# =============================================================

