# perl - CVE-2026-8376 is 32-bit-only (image is amd64/64-bit); the
# archive-tar / IO-Compress issues need running perl on untrusted input, as
# do the newer regex-result (CVE-2026-13221) and S_measure_struct overflow
# (CVE-2026-57432) findings - nothing here runs perl on external input.
# In this image the same CVE IDs also hit the full perl / libperl5.40 /
# perl-modules-5.40 stack pulled in by the git and mariadb-client packages.
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-9538

# util-linux family - CVE-2026-53615 (integer overflow in libblkid DOS
# partition parsing); local, not reachable in this container. Same ID spans
# bsdutils/libblkid1/liblastlog2-2/libmount1/libsmartcols1/libuuid1/login/mount/util-linux.
CVE-2026-53615

# ncurses (libncurses6/libncursesw6/libtinfo6/ncurses-base/ncurses-bin) - CVE-2025-69720
CVE-2025-69720

# gzip - LZH decompressor buffer overflow, needs a crafted archive (1)
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 - symlink traversal via libacl (1)
CVE-2026-54369

# =============================================================
# Introduced by this image's own layer.
# =============================================================

# --- mariadb-client stack (mariadb-client/-core/-common, libmariadb3) ---
# All six CVEs live in the MariaDB *server* source package; Debian marks the
# client binary packages affected because they share the source. This image
# ships no mariadbd.

# Galera/wsrep server-side only (wsrep_notify_cmd RCE, SST donor parameter
# interpolation, wsrep_sst_* global manipulation) - no server, no Galera here.
CVE-2026-49261
CVE-2026-44168
CVE-2026-48163
CVE-2026-48165

# mbstream path traversal - mbstream (mariadb-backup) is not installed in
# this image (verified: no mbstream binary present).
CVE-2026-44171

# mysql_real_escape_string() big5 SQL injection in the client library
# (libmariadb). PHP does not link libmariadb: mysqli/pdo_mysql use the
# bundled mysqlnd (verified in-image). libmariadb3 only backs the `mariadb`
# CLI, an operator inspection tool that does not escape untrusted app input
# with the big5 charset + text protocol combination the CVE requires.
CVE-2026-44172

# --- openssh-client ---
# No sshd in this image; the client is used for operator-configured git+ssh
# deploy remotes only.

# sshd-only: DisableForwarding/PermitTunnel precedence, GSSAPI MaxAuthTries
# DoS - server-side options, no sshd shipped.
CVE-2026-59999
CVE-2026-60000

# Client-side use-after-free during host key re-exchange - requires an
# already-hostile/compromised server changing its host key mid-session; the
# client here only connects to operator-configured trusted deploy hosts.
# No fixed openssh package in trixie yet; drop once Debian ships one.
CVE-2026-60002

# --- supercronic (static Go binary) ---
# Go stdlib os.Root symlink-following traversal, fixed in newer Go patch
# releases; the latest supercronic release is still built on an affected
# toolchain. supercronic only opens operator-configured crontab paths, so
# the traversal is not attacker-reachable here. Drop once a supercronic
# release built on a fixed Go ships.
CVE-2026-39822
